- Public API ---
Translate Vietnamese (or mixed VN/EN) text to English.
Already-English text passes through verbatim (the LLM is instructed to).
Mixed input is fully Englishified — the LLM judges, no client heuristic (R4).
@param text — The prompt to translate. Vietnamese Unicode safe.
@returns English text from the LLM.

Expand + translate a short/rough prompt into a richer, detailed English
prompt suitable for FLUX image generation.
@param text — The short prompt (Vietnamese or English).
@returns Richer, detailed English text from the LLM.

Return a capability slot for `cap`. The slot validates the model, routes to
the configured provider, and exposes the curated model list.
@param cap  The capability name (e.g. 'text2img').
@param opts Injectable options — use `providerRun` to supply a mock in tests.

Run ONE text2img generation via the fal queue.
Polls until COMPLETED or until an error occurs; maps fal errors to our
typed ProviderError-shaped throw (JobError-compatible so the poll loop's
asJobError() picks it up with zero edits).
@param input  the RunInput with model + provider-specific fields
@param signal optional AbortSignal from the job loop's per-attempt controller;
              when aborted the loop stops immediately and cancels the fal request

Map a UI aspect-ratio selector to a fal `image_size` enum string.
@param uiValue — one of the recognised aspect keys, a string, or undefined.
  Unrecognised/garbage values safely fall back to `"square"` (1:1) so a
  bad client input can never yield `undefined` or silently trigger fal's
  `landscape_4_3` default — the safe default is always explicit.
@returns a verified fal `image_size` enum string. Default: `"square"` (1:1).

Drive a single job to a terminal outcome through the poll/retry/timeout loop.
@param job  the durable job (carries the idempotency key `jobId`)
@param run  the INJECTED provider call (Phase 7 = the real fal wrapper)
@param opts observers + the idempotency hook

Enqueue one job. The BullMQ jobId is pinned to the durable `jobId` so a
re-add of the same id is DEDUPED by BullMQ (idempotency at the queue layer;
the loop enforces it again at run time).
